---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import NextBand from '../components/NextBand.astro';
import { SITE, UAE_CT } from '../consts';

const updated = '30 July 2026';
const nf = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-AE');
---

<Base
  title="Terms of use"
  description="Terms governing use of the NUMARATECH website, including the limits of the Corporate Tax estimator and the absence of any advisory relationship."
  ownNav={true}
>
  <PageHero
    kicker="Legal / Terms"
    title="The terms you are reading this under."
    lead="These govern the website only. Advisory engagements are governed by the engagement letter we sign with you, and use of the platform by its own licence terms."
    stats={[
      { label: 'Last updated', value: updated },
      { label: 'Applies to', value: 'this website' },
      { label: 'Advice', value: 'none given here' },
      { label: 'Governing law', value: 'United Arab Emirates' },
    ]}
  />

  <section class="nt-section">
    <div class="nt-prose">
      <h2>Nothing on this website is advice</h2>

      <p>
        We are an accounting and tax consultancy, and we do give advice — but
        only under a signed engagement letter, to a client, about their specific
        circumstances.
      </p>

      <p>
        Everything on this website is general information about finance and
        compliance practice in the United Arab Emirates.
        <strong>
          It is not tax, accounting, legal or financial advice. Reading this site,
          using the estimator, or sending us an enquiry does not create a
          professional or advisory relationship between you and us, and does not
          make you a client.
        </strong>
      </p>

      <p>
        An advisory relationship begins only when both you and
        {' '}{SITE.legalName} have signed an engagement letter setting out the
        scope of the work, and it extends no further than that scope. Until then,
        do not act on anything here without taking advice on your own position.
      </p>

      <p>
        We are accounting and tax consultants. We are not your statutory auditor
        — a firm that prepares the records cannot independently audit them — and
        we are not a law firm. Where a question falls outside what we are
        qualified to answer, we will say so.
      </p>

      <h2>The Corporate Tax estimator</h2>

      <p>
        The estimator on this site is an illustration. It applies the headline
        rate of {UAE_CT.standardRate * 100}% and the {UAE_CT.currency}
        {' '}{nf.format(UAE_CT.zeroBandCeiling)} zero band to figures you type
        in, and optionally models a Small Business Relief election.
      </p>

      <p>Specifically, it does <strong>not</strong> take account of:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>free zone status or qualifying income tests;</li>
        <li>tax groups, consolidation or group relief;</li>
        <li>interest deduction limitation rules;</li>
        <li>tax losses carried forward or back;</li>
        <li>foreign tax credits or double tax treaty relief;</li>
        <li>transfer pricing adjustments;</li>
        <li>
          any relief, exemption or adjustment other than the zero band and Small
          Business Relief;
        </li>
        <li>
          whether the conditions for any relief it does model are actually met in
          your case.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Its output is not a computation of your liability and must not be used
        as one, relied on for filing, or presented to any authority. Statutory
        parameters change; while we intend to keep them current, you must verify
        them against the Federal Tax Authority's published guidance. Your actual
        liability is determined under the applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy</h2>

      <p>
        We take care over what we publish, but we do not warrant that this site
        is accurate, complete or current. Content describing our products
        reflects our intentions at the time of writing and may change without
        notice. Nothing here is an offer capable of acceptance, and nothing here
        forms part of any contract unless we have written it into a signed
        agreement.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>

      <p>You agree not to:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          use this site unlawfully, or in a way that damages it or degrades it
          for others;
        </li>
        <li>
          attempt to gain unauthorised access to any part of the site, its
          hosting or any connected system;
        </li>
        <li>
          scrape, mirror or systematically extract content except as a
          conventional search engine does;
        </li>
        <li>
          use the contact form to send unsolicited marketing, or to send content
          that is unlawful or abusive.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Found a security issue? Please tell us at
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> before disclosing it
        elsewhere. We will acknowledge you and work with you in good faith.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>

      <p>
        The content, design, wordmark and code of this site belong to
        {' '}{SITE.legalName} or our licensors. You may read, print and share
        pages for your own reference or within your organisation. You may not
        republish our content commercially, or present it as your own, without
        our written permission.
      </p>

      <h2>Links out</h2>

      <p>
        Where we link to another site, we do so because we think it is useful. We
        do not control it and are not responsible for its content or its
        handling of your data.
      </p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>

      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, we exclude liability for any
        loss arising from use of, or reliance on, this website or anything on it
        — including any use of the estimator. Nothing in these terms limits
        liability that cannot lawfully be limited, including liability for fraud
        or fraudulent misrepresentation.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability</h2>

      <p>
        We may change, suspend or withdraw this site or any part of it at any
        time, without notice. We do not guarantee uninterrupted availability.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>

      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the United Arab Emirates as
        applied in the Emirate of Dubai, and the courts of Dubai have exclusive
        jurisdiction over any dispute arising from them.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>

      <p>
        We may revise these terms. The version published here is the one that
        applies to your use of the site, so please check the date above.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>

      <p>
        Questions about these terms:
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <NextBand
    title="Need something clarified?"
    body="If any part of these terms is unclear, or you need them in a form your own counsel can review, ask us."
    cta="Email us"
    href="/contact/"
  />
</Base>
